    "q-132987": {
      "dom_id": "question-132987",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the root of the function $g(x)?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The root is at $x\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The roots are the solutions to the equation $g(x)=0,$ which we solve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =0 \\\\ 2x-6 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =6 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has the single root $x=3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
